Each iteration increases i by 1 and thus decreases n-i . Second, we prove $P \wedge B \Rightarrow T > 0$ , by transforming $P \wedge B$ to $T > 0$ .

$$
\begin{array}{l} 0 \leq i \leq n \wedge p = i \cdot x \wedge i \neq n \\ \Rightarrow \quad \langle \mathrm {W e a k e n i n g} \rangle \\ i < n \\ = \quad \langle \mathrm {A r i t h m e t i c} \rangle \\ 0 < n - i \\ = \quad \langle \mathrm {D e f i n i t i o n o f} T \rangle \\ 0 < T \\ \end{array}
$$

